int 3{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=3\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})=-3{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨2{t}^{2}-t,\\,3{e}^{-t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4},\\,(-3{e}^{-t}){|}_{0}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{2}{3}(64)-\\frac{1}{2}(16))-0,\\,(-3{e}^{-4})-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{128}{3}-8),\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{104}{3},\\,3(1-{e}^{-4})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-349125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{104}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349125" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349125" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-3e^{-4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi /4)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0),\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi /4)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\text{ }\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0,\\,1-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\sqrt{2},\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\sqrt{2},\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,\\,1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{16}⟨\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\sqrt{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{16}⟨\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\sqrt{t-1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{16}\\sqrt{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{16},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{(t-1)^{3}}}{3}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{16}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{1},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{(16-1)^{3}}}{3}-\\frac{2\\sqrt{(1-1)^{3}}}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\sqrt{15}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{6},\\,15\\sqrt{10}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{5},\\,15\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{5}{6},\\,10\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-123520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{6}{5},\\,10\\sqrt{15}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3(t-1)^{2},4\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3(t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (4{t}^{3}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{4}-t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨{((1)-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{4}-(1)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩"] ["math" "⟨{(t-1)}^{4}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-4⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{3}+2,\\,{t}^{4}{-}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,0⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\sqrt{t}+t,\\,{2}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (\\sqrt{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {2}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,0⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{2(1)^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{{2}^{1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\frac{7}{6}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=\\frac{5}{6}$ and ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$ Consequently\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,{2}^{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-99586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}+3{t}^{2}+5}{6},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t}-2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{4}{t+1}\\,,3\\sqrt{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,2{t}^{\\frac{3}{2}}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+{c}_{1},\\,2(0)^{\\frac{3}{2}}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+2,\\,2{t}^{3/2}-1⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\ln(t+1)+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349355" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t\\sqrt{t}-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩ \\\\ ⟨8+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-6$ and ${c}_{2}=0.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\ln(t+1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨4,\\,-2⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨4,\\,-2⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨4,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨4,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=3$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡(t)+3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-1⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\csc(t)+3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "q-347095" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sin(3t)-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c90e7b8473ca00d8d2ba74c481b79cbbc48481ed28ed7e46872ca92537cb737"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "ec683e0e44404b80ace907bb8362259b54d74de85f7391fcfcca3993673ae482"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "ec683e0e44404b80ace907bb8362259b54d74de85f7391fcfcca3993673ae482"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "63f6e79a69492d8dcdd580a66b619986cee3548f49cd7f536b8ba6b51b68a66c"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "63f6e79a69492d8dcdd580a66b619986cee3548f49cd7f536b8ba6b51b68a66c"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "e06cc9fbe8326e46624ec2b01d77e0253032f85aecbe56ee77695764d60d3c71"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "e06cc9fbe8326e46624ec2b01d77e0253032f85aecbe56ee77695764d60d3c71"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "6012dbcb57e1484eacbc19e8f20cbb775bab59b29682f455a53c4b90bc903124"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "6012dbcb57e1484eacbc19e8f20cbb775bab59b29682f455a53c4b90bc903124"}] "usage" {"e-615" [] "q-50202" [] "q-80460" [] "e-612" [] "e-613" [] "e-614" [] "q-50204" []} "basis" 1275 "retractions" [[17592186097225 :question/problem "If $F^{′}(t) = ⟨e^{t} - 4, \\sin t⟩$, then $F(t) =$"] [17592186097285 :question/problem "If $F^{′}(t) = ⟨3t^{2}, e^{t}⟩$, then $F(t) =$"] [17592186097226 :question/problem "Find $∫⟨e^{t}, \\cos t⟩dt$."] [17592186096464 :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle$."] [17592186096464 :question/worked-solution "Note that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫⟨6t^{5} + 2t, \\sec^{2} t⟩dt &= ⟨∫(6t^{5} + 2t)dt, ∫\\sec^{2} tdt⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨t^{6} + t^{2} + c_{1}, \\tan t + c_{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨t^{6} + t^{2}, \\tan t⟩ + ⟨c_{1}, c_{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨t^{6} + t^{2}, \\tan t⟩ + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."] [17592186096465 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,$."] [17592186096465 :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n∫⟨\\cos (2t + 1), 4⟩dt = ⟨∫\\cos (2t + 1)dt, ∫4dt⟩\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1)$, we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1$. Then\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u$.\nTherefore, we have\n$∫x(t)dt|= ∫\\cos (2t + 1)dt; = ∫\\cos u \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du; = \\frac{1}{2}∫\\cos udu; = \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin u) + c_{1}; = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (2t + 1) + c_{1}$.\n- For $y(t) =4$, we have\n$∫y(t)dt = ∫4dt = 4t + c_{2}$.\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫⟨\\cos (2t + 1), 4⟩dt &= ⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (2t + 1) + c_{1}, 4t + c_{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (2t + 1), 4t⟩ + ⟨c_{1}, c_{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (2t + 1), 4t⟩ + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096466 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t$."] [17592186096466 :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}⟨2e^{t}, 6t^{2}⟩dt &= ⟨∫_{0}^{2}2e^{t}dt, ∫_{0}^{2}6t^{2}dt⟩. \\\\\n&= ⟨2e^{t} \\mid _{0}^{2}, 2t^{3} \\mid _{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨[2e^{2} - 2e^{0}], [2 \\cdot 2^{3} - 0]⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2e^{2} - 2, 16⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096467 :question/problem "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\, \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle$."] [17592186096467 :question/worked-solution "Note that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\, \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫⟨\\sec t\\tan t, \\sin (2t)⟩dt &= ⟨∫\\sec t\\tan tdt, ∫\\sin (2t)dt⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\sec t + c_{1},-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos (2t) + c_{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(0) = ⟨\\sec 0 + c_{1},-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos (2 \\cdot 0) + c_{2}⟩ &= ⟨0, 0⟩ \\\\\n⟨1 + c_{1},-\\frac{1}{2} + c_{2}⟩ &= ⟨0, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and\n\n$$\nc_2=\\dfrac 12\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle \\sec t - 1, \\, -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095708 17592186095709 17592186095710 17592186095711 17592186095712 17592186095714 17592186095715 17592186095716 17592186095717 17592186095718 17592186096068 17592186096069 17592186096070 17592186096071 17592186096072] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095707 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095707 :answer-field/id] [17592186095707 :answer-field/key] [17592186095707 :answer-field/type] [17592186095713 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095713 :answer-field/id] [17592186095713 :answer-field/key] [17592186095713 :answer-field/type] [17592186096067 :answer-field/correct] [17592186096067 :answer-field/id] [17592186096067 :answer-field/key] [17592186096067 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
